        "output_name": "track_01_batch_story",
        "prompt": "In the last week of autumn, the Japanese garden becomes quiet and almost weightless beneath the falling ginkgo leaves. Their yellow color is not scattered like many European autumn trees, but gathered into one unified golden presence, covering the ground like a soft memory. The pond, the stones, the moss, and the curved branches all seem to hold their breath as the season prepares to end. This batch explores that late-autumn atmosphere through different Asian-oriented instruments, so we can listen to which timbres the model handles most convincingly. Each piece stays simple and focused, allowing one main instrument to carry the feeling of the garden.",
